  "GoNextToDataFinder": "With the data finder, you can select a datetime range while seeing when and how much data is being imported.BREAK_LINEBREAK_LINEIf data are exist, the corresponding cell is displayed in blue; the greater the amount of data, the brighter the blue. The existence of this data refers to the data for the process selected first in the step \"Select target variable\" or the process specified as theSPAN_TAG\"Start point\"SPAN_END_TAG",
  "TourWelcomeTitle": "Welcome to the Analysis Platform",
  "TourWelcome": "In this tour, we are going to walk through the basics of how to run the visualizations. All visualizations can be used in the similar manner.",
  "TourWelcomeQuit": "Quit tour",
  "TourSelectTargetVarTitle": "Select a process and then select some variables that you would like to visualize. You can select additional process by clicking the + button on the upper right.BREAK_LINEYou can also set variables for label plots and facets.BREAK_LINE",
  "TourSelectTargetPeriodTitle": "Marktímabil",
  "TourSelectTargetPeriodDatePickerTitle": "Clicking on the textbox will show datetime selector. You can specify the datetime range with this selector, or by typing directly with the keyboard.",
  "TourFindDataTitle": "No problem. Clicking the \"Data Finder\" button, you can access data finder, which you can find the time range of the stored data.",
  "TourWithDatafinderTitle": "With the data finder, you can select a datetime range while seeing when and how much data is being imported.BREAK_LINEBREAK_LINEIf data are exist, the corresponding cell is displayed in blue; the greater the amount of data, the brighter the blue. The existence of this data refers to the data for the process selected first in the step \"Select target variable\" or the process specified as theSPAN_TAG\"Start point\"SPAN_END_TAG",
